    "type_designations": ["WPI-700", "WPI-701", "WPI-702"],
    "module_designation": null,
    "description": "Indicating device designated WPI-700, designed to be used as part of a Class III or IIII non-automatic weighing instrument designated WPI-701 (single scale) and WPI-702 (dual scale). Operates as single or dual interval, self-indicating, mains-powered, may include a labeller. Main features: processor and converter unit comprising Teraoka TPB-2930 CPU and Teraoka TPB-03324 6-wire A/D converter; colour TFT-LCD touch screen; waterproof metallic enclosure. Devices: initial zero setting, semi-automatic zero setting, zero tracking, semi-automatic subtractive tare weighing, determination and indication of stability of equilibrium, zero indicator, PLUs, preset tare, price calculation, dual scale operation (WPI-702). Interfaces: load cell 6-wire connection, Ethernet, USB. Legal software version 2.xx.xx.xxxx with metrological code in DPS700.dll protected by checksum; alternative World View software (HeaderDisplay.dll version 1.0.0.10, DPS710.dll version 1.0.0.29) permits use for direct sales to the public. Calibration/configuration password-protected and gated by A/D switch inside the enclosure. An alternative construction (modified A/D board TPB-03484, Commel LV-67H main board, CIT-400W-Micro-ATX-Silent-PSU power supply) is also covered."
  },
